  "title": "DHCPv4: Work around non RFC 3925 compliant Option 124 implementations",
  "description": "RFC 3925 indicates that each vendor-class-data instance has its own\nlength, but in practice some vendors have only included the overall\nper-enterprise option length. A recent thread on the dhcp m-l\nclarified this:\nhttps://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/dhcwg/B4fNsvUR0EHxcrKDsKCf7lBrc3s/\n\nWork around noncompliant implementations by checking if the length\nbyte of the vendor-class-data would run past the length of the entire\nper-enterprise option and adding the entire remaining data if so.\nAdd an expert info about noncompliant data, as done in the related issue\nwith option 77 (#16349).\n\nSee also commit dda82d111acecb3c743044bff411f1c4186aa9d7\n\nFix #20097",
